  "photo_observations": {
    "应答器.jpg": "Visible grey box with yellow lid and four lid screws, occupying the bay between adjacent sleepers. The lower body descends beside the sleeper to the deck level; the image does not show the box seated on a sleeper. The yellow lid may overhang the body. Perspective and occlusion prevent calibrated millimetre measurement.",
    "图片15.png": "Several yellow-lid devices are visible between track rails; no unique mapping to model names 02/03 or CAD station handles.",
    "图片17.png": "Repeated grey/yellow boxes are visible in successive separated rail bays; no scale or unique station identifiers.",
    "图片18.png": "Multiple boxes visible in the main-rail corridor; spacing, exact source station and handedness are not dimensioned."
  },
  "conclusion": "No unique CAD-to-balise02/03 body/installation mapping was established by this all-record textual search, full instance inventory, reviewed annotation/registry text and actual source photographs. This is not a proof that an unlabelled balise drawing is absent from the CAD. Source sleeper/rail geometries do supply checkable bay and corridor constraints.",
  "candidate_basis": "Between-sleeper, deck-level mounting is photo-supported. Preserve the inherited 122x116x60 mm body and complete lid/screw assembly, offer 90-degree rigid yaw so the shorter 116-mm axis fits the approximately120-mm source bay, and place the full assembly inside the finite source rail corridor. Exact yaw, bay, lateral position and dimensions remain unconfirmed engineering choices.",
  "as_built_confirmed": false
}
